# Python venv for the C extractor toolchain (tree-sitter; ADR-001) — provisioned per-environment
.venv/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS
.DS_Store

# scratch / throwaway probes
scratch_*.py

# Personal working notes — not source state
notes/

# Run-workspace cloned repos: reproducible by re-cloning the source (clone.py); not source state
runs/*/repo/
runs/*/.clone_descriptor.json

# Generate backend runs index (TASK-050): a run_id→working_path pointer log rebuilt per env
runs/.runs_index.jsonl

# Frontend (TASK-051) build/install artifacts — reproducible from package.json
app/frontend/node_modules/
app/frontend/dist/
# cred.env: a secret token — NEVER commit
cred.env

# NOTE: registry_repo/ is intentionally NOT ignored — it travels to the VDI as the push-ready
# registry tree. It is a generated copy of core/ + overlays/ + docs; after ANY change under
# those, refresh it with `python core/scripts/publish_registry.py --stage registry_repo --force`
# (the §10-gated rebuild) before committing, or it goes stale.

# Mutable build state (D-A22) — everything under cache/ except its README
cache/*
!cache/README.md

# ── run workspaces (TASK-127) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A run workspace is mostly a COPY: core/, the overlay wrappers and prompts are the
# registry hydrated into it, and repo/ is a clone. Tracking those duplicated 137 files
# that already exist elsewhere in this repo — and a duplicate is a drift vector, which is
# exactly how registry_repo/ ended up holding retired skills.
#
# What IS tracked is the evidence a run cannot regenerate: the ledger, the SI artifacts and
# their freeze record, the plan and its trace, the manifest, the per-artifact indexes and
# the code map. That is what `docs/ACCEPTANCE_SI.md` points at.
runs/*/core/
runs/*/.claude/
runs/*/prompts/
runs/*/repo/
runs/*/CLAUDE.md
runs/*/context_set/**/*.pdf
runs/*/context_set/**/*.html
